        {
          "slug": "why-is-lenz-s-law-energy-conservation",
          "title": "Why is Lenz's law energy conservation?",
          "tag": "WHY",
          "summary": "Flips the induced current's direction and gets a perpetual-motion machine (spec below)",
          "sections": "XII 6.5",
          "extension": false,
          "order": 2,
          "spec": "Drop: a magnet falls through a coil; the induced current repels it and the fall slows. Flip: reverse the current's sign and the magnet accelerates, its energy growing forever. Ledger: the slowing magnet's lost KE equals the heat in the coil. Rule: the induced current always opposes the change in flux.",
